 "notes": "Source: Vaithiyam et al., J Lab Physicians 2020;12(3):196-202, AIIMS New Delhi medicine wards & ICU. Text extracted via pypdf (no page-image OCR needed; born-digital PDF). Data taken from Table 4 (Gram-negative) and Table 5 (Gram-positive), both explicitly headed 'Antimicrobial RESISTANCE patterns (%)'. ALL values are %R and were converted to %S = 100 - R (from_R:true on every cell). Confirmation that columns are resistance: colistin = 0 for all GNB, matching narrative 'colistin (no resistance)', and A. baumannii shows ~99-100 for cipro/cefotaxime/ceftazidime consistent with the reported 89% P-XDR. NOTE: the page-4 narrative loosely quotes the resistance numbers ('susceptibility to ... cefoperazone/sulbactam (34.7%)' and 'imipenem (43%)') while actually citing the %R table values — the tables are the authoritative resistance figures used here. n per organism from Table 2 (A.baumannii 92, K.pneumoniae 86, E.coli 75, P.aeruginosa 22, E.faecium 15, S.aureus 10; note isolate counts differ slightly from Table 4/5 denominators as tables include NT cells). Cef-Sul = cefoperazone/sulbactam (non-canonical; token cefoperazonesulbactam). 'Peni'=penicillin (token penicillin). NT (not tested) c",
